DESCRIPTION:In the decades following World War II\, American social scient
 ists turned to the study of Japanese society as an emerging ally and fello
 w capitalist democracy. At a time when influential theories of modernizati
 on predicted the decline of kinship\, community\, hierarchy\, and collecti
 ve obligation\, Japan presented a puzzle. It was an advanced industrial an
 d capitalist society in which village\, family\, corporate welfare\, and m
 oral persuasion in public institutions played powerful roles in organizing
  e\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-11-04 12:18 PST
