SUMMARY:[Stanford Humanities Center / Clayman Institute for Gender Researc
 h] The Queer Thing about Sin | Harry Tanner
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T190000
DTSTAMP:20261104T201802Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54177973515462-54177973515463@local-events
DESCRIPTION:In The Queer Thing About Sin (Bloomsbury 2025)\, Harry Tanner 
 reveals the ancient origins of homophobia. By the end of the 5th century B
 CE\, Greek plays were being staged which ridiculed homosexuality\, by the 
 end of the next century Athenians were being tried for homosexuality and P
 lato had explicitly condemned it in his Laws. In Rome\, the legal situatio
 n was hardly better and in the law codes of Leviticus same-sex sex is cond
 emned. Why did this come to happen\, and what warnings does it hold for u
 \n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://shc.stanford.edu/stanford-humanities-c
 enter/events/harry-tanner-queer-thing-about-sin\nLast synced: 2026-11-04 1
 2:18 PST
